    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6959" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cassĭŏpē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κασσιόπη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Corcyra</i>, now <i>Cassopo</i> or <i>Cassiope</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				16, 9, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				19, § 52</span></i>.—Called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cassĭŏpa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i><span class="en">Gell. 19,
				1, 1</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cassĭŏpĭcus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>of Cassiope</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">filix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					27, 9, 55, § 80</span></i>
			.</div>
